# Copy to .env.local for development, or set these in your host's environment.
# The app starts without any of them and degrades honestly: panels whose
# upstream is unreachable say so rather than rendering blank or inventing a
# number. Everything not listed here is free and keyless.

# --- The Graph Token API -----------------------------------------------------
# Issued at https://thegraph.market, NOT at Subgraph Studio. A Studio gateway
# key answers 401 here. The market issues two forms that are not interchangeable
# at the wire: a key prefixed `server_` authenticates on the X-Api-Key header, a
# JWT on Authorization: Bearer. The client sniffs the prefix, so paste either.
# Without this, the exchange flow desk falls back to archive JSON-RPC and the
# ownership panels are unavailable.
GRAPH_TOKEN_API_KEY=

# Optional. The default host is dropped at the TLS handshake on some networks
# while the same service answers fine at token-api.service.pinax.network. Set
# this only if you hit that; leave it unset in production.
# GRAPH_TOKEN_API_BASE=

# --- The Graph decentralised gateway -----------------------------------------
# API key from Subgraph Studio, used for the Uniswap v3 subgraph queries behind
# the onchain venue panel and the assistant's subgraph tool.
GRAPH_SUBGRAPH_KEY=

# --- Assistant ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint that supports tool calling.
# Without a key the assistant is disabled and the rest of the terminal is
# unaffected.
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Optional second provider, used when the primary is rate limited or down.
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL accepts a comma separated list tried in order, because a
# single free endpoint is not reliable enough to be a fallback on its own.
LLM_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=
LLM_FALLBACK_KEY=
LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Replaces the public archive RPC pool used when the Token API is unavailable.
# The public endpoints rate limit hard; a dedicated one is steadier.
# NETFLOW_RPC_ETH=
